<meta name="description" content="Updated: April 2024 DEFINITIONS The Federal Advisory Committee Act (FACA) as amended (5 U.S.C. Appendix 2): The law outlining how agencies create and manage Federal advisory committees. Congress passed the FACA in 1972. The law ensures that advisory committees provide objective advice to the agencies they serve. It also ensures that the public can access that information. The" />
